# Ignore Rules

## Context
- Defines what files should be ignored by git and cursor
- Prevents sensitive or unnecessary files from being tracked
- Maintains clean project structure

## Requirements
- Ignore environment-specific files
- Ignore Python cache and build artifacts
- Ignore sensitive data and API keys
- Ignore system and IDE files

## Implementation
.gitignore:
```
# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python
build/
develop-eggs/
dist/
downloads/
eggs/
.eggs/
lib/
lib64/
parts/
sdist/
var/
wheels/
*.egg-info/
.installed.cfg
*.egg

# Environment
.env
.venv
env/
venv/
ENV/

# IDE
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
.cursor/logs/

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
```

.cursorignore:
```
# Build and cache
__pycache__/
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/

# Environment and secrets
.env
.venv/
env/
venv/

# Large files and data
data/large/
*.zip
*.tar.gz

# Logs and temporary files
logs/
tmp/
.cursor/logs/
```

## Examples
<example>
# Good: Specific ignore patterns
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.env
.cursor/logs/
</example>

<example type="invalid">
# Bad: Too broad patterns
*.log
temp*
*_old
</example>
